        <p>Sde There is no doubt that we live in an ago of exciternent,and as the struggle for existence is but conducive to good digestion or an appetite trfrispit relish anything, the palate of the average wer,7,etf,co individual has to be tickled and tempted in a ways, We are often lectured about the evil effec7oswo over-indulgence in tea or coffee,not to mention irl,"Dat," ting liquors, until many people are bewildered rdeS.;,l turn to for a beverage, which shall be at once erg.:, 0.2/ to the taste, and supply the desired nourisintrw stimulating qualities. Public attention has bfP. drawn to the merits of Dr. Tibbles' Vi-Cocoa, 45,7110,:fr ing a long felt want in this direction. It is nc"4 a cocoa, but a preparation of two or three otbe'docrge dients, which gives it great nutritive and invig,",/et9 qualities. It is, therefore, not merely a pleasant D'os '5l but a food and a tonic in the bargain. Its suCepollti, certainly been phenomenal, and that is perhaPo ttot to/ , warranty for the claim made on its behalff 0: Cocoa" has the refreshing properties of nee -001/`rsil, ' wourishment of the best cocoas, a tonic and red Live force possessed by neither, and can be tge cases wheie tea and coffee are prohibited." • Dr. Tibbles' Vi-Cocna is neither a medicine oTho 1,0 thirst-assuager. It is a food at the same time "jet a beverage, and thus answers a double purP(''t rel,oo building up of the human constitution, and Intl,:,‘GrPoo it highly serviceable to everybody,eipecially in mills and shops of various kinds among vi -t ted has hitherto been 60 excessively drunk ; Wh further advantage apparently of being easilY 0, or and of agreeing with the most delicate stornaco tle Dr. Tibbles' Vi-Cocoa, 6d., 91., and is. c tained from all Chemiscs,Grocers and Stores.°l.test 61, and 62, Bimini' Row, London, EC. M merit,a dainty sample tin of Dr. Tibbles' be sent free on application to any address,if 0, ing (a postcard will do), the reader will name t rington Examiner." ile I digei</p