        <p>THE Warring/on and Mid-Cheshire Examiner pub- lish d Saturday morning. The district sovered by the Paper comprises many populous manufacturing towns and villages, and a la' ge agricultural tract. THE Earlestown and Newton Examiner and Ashton Colborne, and Haydock Reporter, published Friday afternoon. The district is in the heart of the Lancashire coal field. THE St. Helens Examiner and Prescot Weekly News published Friday afternoon. The district ccmprises the centre of the Mass, Chemical, and Watch Trades of the King- dom, ,kc. rr HE Runcorn Examiner, published Friday after noon. It is the only Weekly Paper in the district. an offers the best and cheapest facilities to advertisers. rr HE Widnes Examiner, published Friday after noon. Widnes contains the largest number of Chemiea Works of any town in the kingdom, and is rapidly becoming an important centre of industry.</p>
        <p>Auction, Education, Wanted, To be Let, On Sale, Lega Public Meeting, Sermon, Lecture, Bazaar, and other Public Notices, Advertisements (exc,pt Parliamentary) are inserted all the above papers at one charge.</p>
        <p>Each of the above papers consists of 8 pages, 56 long and wide columne,each column admitting more matter than the columns of any other local paper—a fact deserving the atten tion of both advertisers and subscribers. Each Examzu in dition to giving the local intelligence of the district, in which it circulates, contains the general news of the week. j Price of each Paper—ONE PENNY.</p>
