      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-06-17_WidnesExaminer_art0072" n="art0072">
        <head>FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>THE NORTHERN UNION.</p>
        <p>TEM NEW RULES ON PROFESSIONA.LISq• A wen-attended meeting of the committee governing the Northern Union was held on Friday evening last week at fluddersfield,Mr. J. E. Warrm, Warring,ton, in the chair. The principal business was the further con- sideratinn of the scheme of professionalism framed be the Profejjonai S lb-Committee and provisionally adopted at the last meetict of the committee at Man- the3ter, aril the addition of a couple of clauses to Rule nne. 1; was decided to add to rule 1, clause " D "as I°llews :—"Any professional player thrown out of work through fire, lock-our, or strike, permission may be given to s'ich olaver to play football at the discretion of the Nuthern Rugby Union Committee."—To the same rule,. was also decided to add Clause " E " as follows : —" Immediately a player loses or chancres his situation the secretary of the club to which he is attached nnet notify the same to the hen, secretary of the Union, and such player must not play football until he is again in bona-fi Jo work, and particulars of which have been given to the secretary of the Union.—The following ad- dition was made Co By-law 12 of the 'Union :—" The committee of the Union shall have the right of placing anon the agenda any proposed amendment or alteration 'of bv-laws."—A new by-law was added as follows : " The Northern Union Committee shall have power to deal with any off.nding club or clubs,player or players. as they may think fit,and also to deal with any matter that may arise and not provided for in these rules,"</p>
        <p>LA.TCRFOUD GOOD TEIPLADB, The weekly meeting of the Good Templars' Lodge was held in the Temperance Hall, Latchford, on Monday evening. Bro. Walker, C.T., occupied the chair. The eoening ceremonies were gone through, after which Bro. Cotterill. of Stockton Bresth, and Bro. Ellison gave short addresses. The programme consisted of a series or questions supplied by Bro. A. Ford. which caused quite an amusing debate be- tween Bros. IL Blease and 11. Richardson. A rote of thanks to Bro. Ford brought a pleasant meeting to a close,</p>
      </div>
