      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-06-17_WidnesExaminer_art0074" n="art0074">
        <head>BOWLIN G.</head>
        <p>BOWLIN G.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE couNry ASSOCIATION. SECoND ROUND. WARRINGTON SOUTg v. STMITFORD.—These affiliated dis- tricts played la the second round of the championship com- petition over the ariffia green, Lower Broughton, on Satur- day. It was a eap,tal contest from beginning to end, and though the Stretford players chimed a majority of wins several of the Warringtonians had gained such substantial Majorities that at the close they were able to claim a victory by five points. The op-fling quartette saw Warr ington win' ! ning three oat of four games played, T Hackett gaining the most decisive win of the afternoon, taking an early lead and distancing his opponent by 14 shots. J Gleans never allowed his opponent a chance alter the 15th end, and his victory of ten points was well earned. It Fairbrother also displayed his usual consistent good fiirm, and the issue of his game with A. Twiss was never in doubt, and the nine points victory wns never in doubt, and the nine points viotory was well deserved. A sequence of god woods gave r Drink- water a substantial lead in his game with T Bolton. so that the Warringtoninn never got on equal terms, and the close saw the Stretford man victorious by seven points. Thus ' when the next set of players appeared Watring,ton had a lead of 26 points. Alter giving e ley pr miss, S. Massey failed at tee sixteenth end, and J. Whitehead with a sequence of capital woods won his game by eight points. H. Fogg counter-balanced this defeat by disposing of his opponent in a quickly played match, the game only extending over 21 ends, the final score reading 21-14. B Shaw experienced an unexpected reve^se at the hands of D Wigglesworth, and J Swanton also failed to account for S Allsopp, so that Warring- ton's majority was now reduced to ten points. F Berry.after establishing 'a substantial load over 0 Kulow, allowed his opponent to peel at the 27th end, and the Stretford player eventually won by three joints. A welcome victory was scored by J Show, and Warrington's hopes were in the ascendent when T Locker appeared to have his game with 16 D Lowe la safe keeping. The Stretford man played up pluckily, and securing the jack at the 28th end, when Locker was one short of a game, eventually ran out the winner by a single point. T.Davies was a long way in arrears at the opening of his match with J. Poynton, but he subsequently got sufficient points to make the match secure for Watrington, who eventually won, as stated above, by five points. Details ;</p>
